## Context

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) merges reports on their subject alone. The [review of #4471](/kb/reviews/4471/) shows why that loses causal distinctions. The subject is a retrieval hint, not an identity for a defect.

## Proposed decision

1. Deduplicate export rows by report ID, rejecting conflicting copies for investigation.
2. Resolve the tenant and its actual locale and form version. Do not substitute browser locale or the intake tag for tenant configuration.
3. Establish the mechanism using channel and the supplied cause logic, corroborated by the report and reproducible cases.
4. Merge reports only when the same evidenced cause applies. Keep one engineering ticket per confirmed mechanism and link every counted report ID.
5. Keep missing tenants and ambiguous descriptions visible for investigation. Do not turn uncertainty into a confirmed new cause or silently discard the report.
6. Recompute counts and review affected cases when source data, tenant configuration or classification logic changes.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences and status

The desk must consult context before merging. Similar wording can stay in different tickets; different wording can belong to one cause. Counts are reproducible and uncertainty is explicit.

This is a proposed replacement, pending the desk owner's acceptance. It does not edit accepted decision 0001 or retrospectively assert that the desk changed its process.

